{
  "$comment": "Single source of truth for every Telegram command this bot responds to. 'local' = handled directly in src/handlers/commands.js (see the case in the switch). 'forward' = relayed as-is to the agent backend, which matches it against a *_INTENT regex in trained-assist-agent/src/runner.js (getQuickAnswer) — see that repo's src/telegram-commands.js for the matching agent-side registry entry. scripts/check-commands-registry.js enforces that every 'local' entry has a real switch case; AGENT_FORWARDED_COMMANDS/ADMIN_FORWARDED_COMMANDS in commands.js are derived from this file, not hand-duplicated. Adding a new command? Add it here in the same PR — that's what keeps this list from drifting out of sync with the code again.",
